s a potentially costly play. My ♠2 remains as a trump card to regain control later or apply pressure. It also allows me to follow up with 555-3 if I gain control (and it\'s a good structure to play).\n\nTherefore, the only right decision is to play the ♥Q, apply immediate pressure and set up opportunities for the rest of the game.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♥Q"]}\n\n\n', 'output': 'Evaluation: I am in the "Upstream" (Shang Jia) position relative to the Landlord, meaning I play immediately before him. My primary role is to block the Landlord\'s small and medium cards to force him to spend high cards (A, 2, Jokers) to regain control. The Landlord played a single 10. I have a single ♥Q which is a perfect blocking card; it beats the 10 and is not part of a pair or triplet I need to preserve. Playing the ♠2 now would be wasteful as it is my only major control card, and breaking the pair of Kings (♣K ♦K) reduces my defensive strength against pairs. Passing would give the Landlord a free turn, which I should avoid as the blocker.\n\nReason: My hand contains a natural single ♥Q that beats the Landlord\'s ♣10. Playing the Q forces the Landlord to use a high card (K, A, 2) or pass, fulfilling my role as the blocker. It preserves my pair of Kings and my ♠2 for later critical moments.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♥Q"]}'}
